{
  "name": "Blog Pipeline Error Alerts",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Blog pipeline error alerts (fix 1 + fix 3)\nSet as `errorWorkflow` on every blog workflow. On any failure: ONE plain line to the Telegram Blog topic (workflow, step, error; <=300 chars; no secrets). Pipeline failures alert once per failed execution (each retry that fails alerts again); other workflows send the same alert at most once an hour.\n\nThe failed run is found by execution id (`blog_runs.last_exec`), never guessed. It is marked `failed` (or `held` when Agent 5's gate held the post). A scheduled run (or its retry) gets up to 2 retries a day, 30 min apart. A queued topic whose run is not retried is marked `failed`. If the post was already published (e.g. the announcement failed), it only alerts.\n\nTest: run with input `{\"dryRun\": true, \"forceFailAt\": \"agent1\"}` (dry runs are marked [test], never write the queue, retry after 1 min).",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 680
      },
      "position": [
        -420,
        -520
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Error Trigger",
      "name": "Error Trigger",
      "parameters": {},
      "position": [
        -200,
        100
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "executeOnce": true,
      "id": "Summarize Failure",
      "name": "Summarize Failure",
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// One plain line: which workflow, which step, what went wrong. No stack traces, no secrets, <= 300 chars.\nconst e = $input.first().json;\nconst wf = (e.workflow && e.workflow.name) || 'unknown workflow';\nconst ex = e.execution || {}, err = ex.error || (e.trigger && e.trigger.error) || {};\nconst step = ex.lastNodeExecuted || (err.node && err.node.name) || (e.trigger ? 'trigger' : 'unknown step');\nlet msg = String(err.message || 'unknown error').split('\\n')[0];\nif (err.description && String(err.description).length < 160 && !msg.includes(err.description)) msg += ' (' + String(err.description).split('\\n')[0] + ')';\nmsg = msg.replace(/\\d{8,10}:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{30,}/g, '<redacted>').replace(/bearer\\s+\\S+/gi, 'Bearer <redacted>')\n  .replace(/((?:api[_-]?key|token|secret|password|key)=)[^&\\s]+/gi, '$1<redacted>').replace(/\\/bot[^\\/\\s]+\\//g, '/bot<redacted>/')\n  .replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\nconst testMarked = /\\[test\\]/i.test(msg);                 // workflows without a blog_runs row mark test failures in the message\nmsg = msg.replace(/\\s*\\[test\\]\\s*/gi, ' ').trim();\nconst short = wf.replace(/^PHASE 5:\\s*/, '').replace(/\\s*\\(.*\\)$/, '').replace(/^Blog\\s+/, '');\nconsole.log('Error alert for', wf, '/', step, '/ execution', ex.id, '/', msg.slice(0, 200));\nreturn [{ json: { wf, short, step, msg, testMarked, mode: ex.mode || (e.trigger && e.trigger.mode) || '', executionId: String(ex.id || ''),\n  isPipeline: /^PHASE 5: Agent [1-5]/.test(wf), isAgent1: /^PHASE 5: Agent 1/.test(wf) } }];\n"
      },
      "position": [
        20,
        100
      ],
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
